{"results":[{"url":"https://www.manchestereveningnews.co.uk/sport/football/football-news/paul-pogba-france-world-cup-34262110","final_url":"https://www.manchestereveningnews.co.uk/sport/football/football-news/paul-pogba-france-world-cup-34262110","title":"What happened to Paul Pogba and reason World Cup winner didn’t make France squad","description":"The former Manchester United midfielder won the World Cup with France in 2018 but is supporting from the sidelines at this summer's tournament","language":"en","text":"## Need to know\n\n# What’s happened to Paul Pogba? Reason why World Cup winner didn’t make France squad\n\n## The former Manchester United midfielder won the World Cup with France in 2018 but is supporting from the sidelines at this summer's tournament\n\nSport\n\n**Ben Pawlowski**\n\n17:30, 09 Jul 2026\n\nPaul Pogba was handed a doping ban in 2023 while playing for Juventus(Image: Valery HACHE / AFP via Getty Images)\n\n### *All you need to know about Paul Pogba's absence from France's World Cup squad*\n\n1. **Missing out:** Paul Pogba was excluded from France's squad for the FIFA World Cup 2026 after being unable to demonstrate his fitness. The seasoned midfielder, 33, acknowledged himself that taking part in this summer's tournament was always an unrealistic aspiration given his significant lack of match sharpness.\n2. **Prolonged absence:** The World Cup 2018 winner had to reconstruct his career after receiving a four-year doping ban in February 2024 after testing positive for \"non-endogenous testosterone metabolites.\" His suspension was subsequently cut to 18 months on appeal by the Court of Arbitration for Sport, who accepted his argument that his ingestion of a banned substance \"was not intentional,\" allowing him to resume playing from March 2025 onwards.\n3. **Injury struggles:** Pogba signed for AS Monaco on a two-year contract in the summer of 2025 following the termination of his deal with Juventus. Yet his comeback to football has been disrupted by ongoing knee problems, resulting in him missing substantial parts of the 2025-26 season and even being omitted from Monaco's Champions League knockout squad.\n4. **Midfield competition:** French manager Didier Deschamps continues to hold the player in high regard, but couldn't warrant selecting him based solely on his previous reputation. The national side possesses remarkable depth in central areas, meaning Pogba required regular game time to have any realistic prospect.\n5. **Distant goal:** Pogba has openly acknowledged his present circumstances, characterising a possible return to the national camp as an \"ultra-bonus\" rather than an immediate priority. He maintains his main concentration at this moment is purely on regaining full fitness and securing regular playing time for his club.\n6. **Adidas ambassador:** Despite being left out of the final squad, the former Manchester United midfielder has nevertheless travelled to the United States this summer. He is currently attending the competition in a promotional role while serving as an official ambassador for sportswear giant Adidas.\n7. **Supporting the team:** He also intends to keenly monitor the French side's journey as a committed supporter rather than a crucial participant. He conveyed a genuine wish to visit the squad and back Deschamps, who is overseeing what is expected to be his concluding major competition for Les Bleus.\n8. **Upcoming quarter-final:** France will be aiming to extend their remarkable campaign without Pogba when they meet Morocco in the quarter-finals on Thursday night. The eagerly awaited clash occurs at Boston Stadium in Massachusetts, representing a rematch of their semi-final four years ago in Qatar.\n\nThousands of Man United fans upgraded their matchday last season. This is how they did it.\n\nThis article contains affiliate links, we will receive a commission on any sales we generate from it. Learn more\n\nVarious Prices\n\nSeat Unique\n\nBuy official packages at Seat Unique\n\nOfficial premium experiences at Old Trafford are available now for the 26/27 Premier League season. Make it easier than ever to turn a regular fixture into something genuinely unforgettable.\n\nFollow men:\n\n* Facebook\n* X (Twitter)\n* Instagram\n\nComments\n\n\n\n\n\n---","author":"Ben Pawlowski","published_date":"2026-07-09T16:30:00Z","latency_ms":1095.2770230005626,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}